If you have access to the source code, look in the shknam.c file.  Basically,  
each type of shop has a particular ethnic type of shopkeeper associated with  
it.  To wit--

Liquor--Ukrainean, North Russian, Swiss
Books--Irish
Armours--Turkish
Wands--Welsh, Scottish
Rings--Dutch, Scandinavian
Foods--Indonesian
Weapons--??  (The program says 'Perigord', and all the names look kind of like  
Provencal to me...)
Tools--?? ('Spmi'--it looks like a bunch of names spelt backwards)
General--'Suriname'(??), Greenland, Northern Canadian, Icelandic

It has a whole list of names for each type, which I could post if there is  
interest...but apparently, except for Tools, it picks them in order through the  
list.  Which means that, unless you run into several stores of the same type,  
you're always going to get 'Tsjernigof', 'Kanturk', 'Kalecik', 'Trallwng',  
'Flugi', 'Tjibarusa', 'Rouffiac', and 'Possogroenoe.'

I personally have also seen: 'Gomel' and 'Ossipewsk'(liquors); 'Rath Luirc',  
'Ennistymon', and 'Lahinch'(books); 'Boyabai' and 'Yildizeli'(armour);  
'Mallwyd'(wands); 'Gheel'(rings); 'Tjiwidej'(foods); 'Lerignac'(weapons); and  
'Asidonhopo', 'Manlobbi', 'Adjama', and 'Pakka Pakka'(general).

Anybody who's gone deeper and encountered more shops has probably seen more  
than these--and if you have, send me a message.  Also send me names of hardware  
shopkeepers--none of the ones in the file look particularly familiar to me, but  
I don't run across hardware stores often.

And if demand warrants, I will post the complete list!  Straight of 3.0j  
sourcecode!
